course: dictionary
lesson: 10185
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. The word till can mean different things, and the words around it tell you which meaning fits. «Muuum, how long till we get there?» Here till means until: it asks how much time is left before we arrive.
explain: Till can also be a noun. A till is the drawer or machine in a shop where money is kept and change is given, also called a cash register. «Pay at the till» means go to that machine to pay. Ask yourself: is this about a time, a place for money, or a job to do?
explain: Till can be a verb too. To till the soil means to dig it and prepare it for planting, so farmers till the land before they sow seeds. Each meaning fits a different sentence, so always check the words around it before you decide.
fact: Till means until, up to a time: open from 9 till 5.
fact: A till is where a shop keeps its money, also called a cash register.
fact: To till the soil means to dig it and prepare it for planting.
fact: Till can be a preposition, a conjunction, a noun or a verb, so check how it is used in the sentence.
fact: In maths, «from 9 till 5» is the time between 9 o'clock and 5 o'clock, which is 8 hours.
exercise: «Muuum, how long till we get there?» What does till mean here? | A drawer where money is kept | To dig and prepare the soil | *Until, up to the time we arrive | A kind of cake
exercise: The farmer will till the field before sowing the seeds. What does till mean? | Until the seeds grow | To ask a question | The machine where the farmer pays | *To dig and prepare the soil for planting
exercise: «Pay at the till, please.» What is a till? | *The drawer or machine where a shop keeps money | A time of day | A tool for digging soil | A bag for shopping
test: The shop is open «from 9 till 5». How many hours is that? | *8 | 10 | 7 | 6
test: «They laugh till they cry.» What does till mean in this sentence? | The drawer where money is kept | A long, thin piece of wood | To dig and prepare the soil | *Until, up to the time they cry
exam: «Saffie gets home at quarter to four to an empty house till six.» What does till mean here? | A type of bread | A machine where money is kept | To prepare the soil for planting | *Until six o'clock
